square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(t+5)^{2}-25 & =-13 \\\\ (t+5)^{2} & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $p=5,$ $q=12,$ and $p+q=17.$" 13194139533394 17592186045585 true] [17592186069027 1068 #edb/ref 17592186065565 13194139533394 17592186045585 false] [17592186069027 1068 #edb/ref 17592186246825 13194139533394 17592186045585 true] [17592186069027 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533394 17592186045585 true] [17592186069027 1071 "$\\displaystyle \\int(5x + 35)/((x + 2)^{2}(x - 3))dx =$\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." 13194139533394 17592186045585 false] [17592186069027 1071 "$\\int \\frac{5x+35}{(x+2)^{2}(x-3)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139533394 17592186045585 true] [17592186069027 1074 "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5x+35}{(x+2)^{2}(x-3)}=\\frac{A}{(x+2)}+\\frac{B}{(x+2)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(x-3)}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,$ $B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x+2)^{2}(x-3)$ and get\n\n$$\n5x+35=A(x+2)(x-3)+B(x-3)+C(x+2)^{2}.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-2,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $C$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(-2)+35 & =A(-2+2)(-2-3)+B(-2-3)+C(-2+2)^{2} \\\\ -10+35 & =B(-5) \\\\ B & =\\frac{25}{-5} \\\\ B & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=3,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $B$ and solve for $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(3)+35 & =A(3+2)(3-3)+B(3-3)+C(3+2)^{2} \\\\ 15+35 & =C{(5)}^{2} \\\\ C & =\\frac{50}{25} \\\\ C & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known values of $B$ and $C,$ we can solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(0)+35 & =A(0+2)(0-3)+B(0-3)+C(0+2)^{2} \\\\ 35 & =-6A-3B+4C \\\\ 35 & =-6A-3(-5)+4(2) \\\\ 35 & =-6A+23 \\\\ 6A & =-35+23 \\\\ A & =\\frac{-12}{6} \\\\ A & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{5x+35}{(x+2)^{2}(x-3)}=-\\frac{2}{(x+2)}-\\frac{5}{(x+2)^{2}}+\\frac{2}{(x-3)}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5x+35}{(x+2)^{2}(x-3)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-\\frac{2}{(x+2)}-\\frac{5}{(x+2)^{2}}+\\frac{2}{(x-3)})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\int \\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int \\frac{1}{(x+2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+\\frac{5}{x+2}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+K,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is an integral constant." 13194139533394 17592186045585 true] [17592186078465 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247243 13194139533394 17592186045585 true] [17592186083238 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247324 13194139533394 17592186045585 true] [17592186083238 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247325 13194139533394 17592186045585 true] [17592186083238 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247326 13194139533394 17592186045585 true] [17592186083312 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247317 13194139533394 17592186045585 true] [17592186083312 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247318 13194139533394 17592186045585 true] [17592186083312 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247319 13194139533394 17592186045585 true] [17592186083312 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247320 13194139533394 17592186045585 true] [17592186083312 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247321 13194139533394 17592186045585 true] [17592186083313 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247316 13194139533394 17592186045585 true] [17592186083316 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247327 13194139533394 17592186045585 true] [17592186083316 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247328 13194139533394 17592186045585 true] [17592186083386 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247099 13194139533394 17592186045585 true] [17592186083387 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247100 13194139533394 17592186045585 true] [17592186087697 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247141 13194139533394 17592186045585 true] [17592186087836 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247343 13194139533394 17592186045585 true] [17592186087850 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247370 13194139533394 17592186045585 true] [17592186087851 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247377 13194139533394 17592186045585 true] [17592186087858 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247332 13194139533394 17592186045585 true] [17592186087858 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247333 1319413953339