n *eigenvector* is simply a generalized eigenvector of rank $1.$\n\nFirst, we compute $A+5I:$\n\n$$\nA+5I=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -7\\end{aligned}]+5[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the image of $v$ under the action of $A+5I:$\n\n$$\n(A+5I)v=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]={{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{w}\\ne 0\n$$\n\n- Since we got a nonzero vector, we now compute the image of $w$ under the action of $A+5I:$\n\n$$\n(A+5I)w=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]={{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}\\ne 0\n$$\n\n- Again, since we got a nonzero vector in the last step, we now compute the image of $x$ under the action of $A+5I:$\n\n$$\n(A+5I)x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=0\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain the following chain of maps:\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{v}\\overset{A+5I\\,}{\\to }{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{w}\\overset{A+5I\\,}{\\to }{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}\\overset{A+5I\\,}{\\to }{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{0}\n$$\n\nHere, we see that $A+5I$ maps $v$ to $0$ in $3$ steps.\n\nTherefore:\n\n$\\,$ *$v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $3$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-5$ of $A.$*\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139533394 17592186045585 true] [17592186162069 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247172 13194139533394 17592186045585 true] [17592186162069 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247173 1319413953