{u}^{2},\\,{v}^{2},\\,u+2v⟩.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since $(4,1,4)$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}=4 \\\\ {v}^{2}=1 \\\\ u+2v=4\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}u=2 \\\\ v=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2v,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=2$ and $v=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(2,1) & =⟨2(2),\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(2,1) & =⟨0,\\,2(1),\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(2,1)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(2,1) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 4 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,-8,\\,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-2,\\,-8,\\,8⟩\\cdot ⟨x-4,\\,y-1,\\,z-4⟩ & =0 \\\\ (-2)\\cdot (x-4)+(-8)\\cdot (y-1)+8\\cdot (z-4) & =0 \\\\ -2x-8y+8z-16 & =0 \\\\ -x-4y+4z-8 & =0 \\\\ x+4y-4z & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533394 17592186045585 true] [17592186172265 1068 #edb/ref 17592186168423 13194139533394 17592186045585 false] [17592186172265 1068 #edb/ref 17592186246981 13194139533394 17592186045585 true] [17592186172265 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533394 17592186045585 true] [17592186172265 1071 "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surfac